From 227e01c4b7254a7b628c76dc89c18380bf0a3ceb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work8_fin_tc <adbtrr_work8_fin_tc@local>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 06:16:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] os/kernel/environ: Add ASSERT hitting test case for
 env_release

env_release() is called from group_leave() when the last member of a
task group exits. It dereferences the "group" argument right after
DEBUGASSERT(group), so a NULL group is a caller contract violation.

Add a negative test case which calls env_release() with a NULL task
group from kernel context so that the assertion in
os/kernel/environ/env_release.c is executed.

 - os/drivers/os_api_test/kernel/test_assert_environ.c : kernel side
   helper reached through the TESTIOC_ASSERT_ENVIRON ioctl.
 - apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/tc_assert_environ.c : user side
   test case. A return from the ioctl is reported as a test case failure.

Controlled by CONFIG_TC_KERNEL_ASSERT_ENVIRON, default n, depends on
CONFIG_DEBUG and on environment variable support. It crashes the board
by design and must be enabled alone.
